# Superpowers (project-local)

This repository vendors [Superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) under `.cursor/skills/superpowers/`.

**Before substantive work**, read and follow the relevant skill:

`.cursor/skills/superpowers/skills/{skill-name}/SKILL.md`

Start with `using-superpowers`, then invoke process skills when they apply (for example `brainstorming` before new features, `systematic-debugging` for bugs, `test-driven-development` during implementation).

## Cursor tool mapping

When a skill references another harness, use Cursor equivalents:

| Skill / doc reference | Cursor |
| --- | --- |
| `Skill` / read a skill | `Read` on `.cursor/skills/superpowers/skills/{name}/SKILL.md` |
| `Bash` | `Shell` |
| `Edit` | `StrReplace` |
| `TodoWrite`, `Task`, `Read`, `Write` | Same names |

## IDE plugin (recommended)

For automatic session bootstrap and hooks, install the marketplace plugin in Cursor Agent chat:

```text
/add-plugin superpowers
```

The vendored copy keeps skills pinned for this repo and works in environments without the plugin (for example Cloud Agents).

## Precedence

Instructions in `AGENTS.md` and direct user messages override skills. Skills override default agent behavior.
